      "mergedPostDetails": "When I select “Create Instance” in the World Details,\n\nselect a group,\n\nset the instance type to “Group (Group Only),”\n\nset the access role for the instance to “All Roles,” and disable avatar performance,\n\nand then actually open the instance and try to invite a friend who belongs to the same group, I get the message “This user is not a member of the group...” and cannot invite them.\n\nStrangely enough, if you select “See All” under “Groups” on the profile screen of the user you’re trying to invite, and then return to the original profile screen, you’ll be able to invite that user.\n\nThis bug began occurring with the most recent update (the one that changed the UI—ver 2026.3.1).\n\n---\n\nDetails\n\nCategory: User Interface\n\nFrequency: always\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: any)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.3.1-1886-a268441585-Release\n\nUnity version: 2022.3.22f2-DWR\n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
